 If verified files overlap existing local edits, Hermes does not overwrite them. It saves the verified patch under `~/.hermes/autopilot/results/<mission-id>/verified.patch` and reports the conflicting paths.
+
+## Inspect versus change
+
+`ha` now detects whether the request should answer a repository question or
+modify files.
+
+```bash
+ha "tell me what this repo does"
+```
+
+Inspection mode creates a sanitized, temporary repository manifest, runs the
+analysis in an isolated mission, prints the independently verified answer, and
+does not add a report file to the source checkout.
+
+```bash
+ha "create a linux directory and add linux/README.md"
+```
+
+Change mode creates, verifies, and safely applies the requested repository
+change. A request containing both inspection and mutation language is treated
+as a change request.
+
+Use `--mode inspect` or `--mode change` to override automatic detection.
+
+## Repositories without a first commit
+
+`ha` works after `git init` even when `HEAD` does not exist. It creates a
+temporary synthetic baseline from the current working tree without moving the
+source branch or making a source commit. Verified changes are applied back to
+the working tree, while inspection leaves the source untouched.
